Real-World Use
Hybrid topology is common in large enterprise networks, where different network sections are connected using different designs.


Physical vs Logical Topology


Physical Topology

Describes how devices and cables are physically connected.

Example:

PCs connected to a central switch.

Logical Topology

Describes how data flows between devices, regardless of the physical arrangement.

This distinction is important because a network can have a physical star arrangement while its logical communication behavior is different.
